# Production Environment Configuration Example
# Use this as a reference for deploying to production

# ⚠️ IMPORTANT: Never commit actual secrets to version control!
# Use your hosting platform's environment variable/secrets management instead.

# ============================================
# BACKEND PRODUCTION (.env.production)
# ============================================

# Database - Use MongoDB Atlas for production
MONGODB_URL=mongodb+srv://production_user:secure_password_here@job-finder-prod.mongodb.net/job_finder?retryWrites=true&w=majority
DB_NAME=job_finder

# JWT - MUST be changed from development!
# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
JWT_SECRET_KEY=generated_very_long_random_secret_key_here_minimum_32_chars
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
JWT_EXPIRY_HOURS=24

# Groq AI - Get from https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_production_groq_api_key_here

# Telegram - Get from @BotFather
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=production_telegram_bot_token_here

# Production URLs
BACKEND_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
FRONTEND_URL=https://yourdomain.com
CORS_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com,https://www.yourdomain.com

# Environment
ENVIRONMENT=production

# Application Limits (adjust based on your needs)
DAILY_APPLICATION_LIMIT=5

# ============================================
# FRONTEND PRODUCTION (.env.production)
# ============================================

# API Configuration - Update to your production backend
VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
VITE_DEBUG=false

# ============================================
# DEPLOYMENT PLATFORM INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================

# --- RENDER (Recommended for Backend) ---
# 1. Go to https://render.com
# 2. Create new Web Service from GitHub
# 3. Select your repository
# 4. Set Build Command: pip install -r requirements.txt
# 5. Set Start Command: gunicorn app.main:app
# 6. Add Environment Variables in Render dashboard:
#    - Copy each variable from above
#    - Set them in Render's "Environment" section
# 7. Deploy!

# --- VERCEL (Recommended for Frontend) ---
# 1. Go to https://vercel.com
# 2. Import your GitHub repository
# 3. Set Framework: React
# 4. Set Build Command: npm run build
# 5. Add Environment Variables in Vercel dashboard:
#    - VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
# 6. Deploy!

# --- RAILWAY (Alternative for Backend) ---
# 1. Go to https://railway.app
# 2. Create new service from GitHub
# 3. Select your repository
# 4. Add variables in Railway dashboard
# 5. Database option: Add MongoDB URI
# 6. Deploy!

# --- MONGODB ATLAS (Database) ---
# 1. Go to https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas
# 2. Create Project and Cluster
# 3. Whitelist IP addresses
# 4. Create Database User (different from account)
# 5. Get connection string and add to MONGODB_URL
# 6. Monitor backups and security

# --- GROQ API (AI Service) ---
# 1. Go to https://console.groq.com
# 2. Create API key for production
# 3. Set usage limits/quotas
# 4. Monitor API costs

# ============================================
# SECURITY CHECKLIST FOR PRODUCTION
# ============================================

# ✅ Before deploying, ensure:
# - [ ] JWT_SECRET_KEY is NOT the development key
# - [ ] All API keys are production keys (not development)
# - [ ] CORS_ORIGINS restricted to your actual domain(s)
# - [ ] ENVIRONMENT=production
# - [ ] MONGODB_URL uses MongoDB Atlas (not local)
# - [ ] .env file is NOT in version control
# - [ ] Secrets stored in hosting platform (not in repo)
# - [ ] Database backups enabled
# - [ ] Domain has HTTPS/SSL certificate
# - [ ] Environment variables are set in deployment platform
# - [ ] Tested with production credentials before final deploy

# ============================================
# MONITORING & MAINTENANCE
# ============================================

# After deployment:
# 1. Monitor error logs
# 2. Check API response times
# 3. Monitor database usage
# 4. Set up alert notifications
# 5. Regular security updates
# 6. Rotate secrets periodically

# ============================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING PRODUCTION ISSUES
# ============================================

# "Database connection failed"
# → Check MONGODB_URL format and IP whitelist in Atlas

# "API key not found or invalid"
# → Regenerate key in respective service console

# "CORS error from frontend"
# → Verify CORS_ORIGINS matches frontend domain

# "Telegram notifications not working"
# → Check TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN is valid
# → Verify user has Chat ID registered

# "Application too slow"
# → Add database indexes
# → Enable caching
# → Horizontal scaling

